# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# stoned.living — Environment Variables
#
# For local development:  copy this file to .env and fill in values
# For Cloudflare Pages:   add these as "Environment Variables" in the dashboard
#                         (Settings → Environment Variables → Production)
# For the Worker:         add secrets via `wrangler secret put SECRET_NAME`
#                         inside /workers/resolver
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Frontend (Cloudflare Pages) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# All VITE_ prefixed variables are inlined at build time.

# The Movie Database (TMDb) — required for catalog, search, and media details
# Get your key at: https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api
VITE_TMDB_API_KEY=""

# TMDb v4 read-access bearer token (JWT) — used instead of API key when present
# Found at: https://www.themoviedb.org/settings/api → Read Access Token
VITE_TMDB_READ_TOKEN=""

# URL of the deployed Cloudflare Worker resolver API
# Example: https://stoned-resolver.YOUR_SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev
# Used by WatchPlayer to resolve .m3u8 stream URLs and by AdminPanel for health checks
VITE_RESOLVER_URL="https://stoned-resolver.workers.dev"

# Firebase configuration — copy from your Firebase project settings
# (Project settings → General → Your apps → Firebase SDK snippet → Config)
VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY=""
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=""
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=""
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=""
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=""
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID=""

# ── Cloudflare Worker (/workers/resolver) ──────────────────────────────────
# These are set on the Worker via `wrangler secret put SECRET_NAME`
# Do NOT prefix with VITE_ — they are never exposed to the browser.

# sportsrc.org API key — primary live sports data source.
# Production:  cd workers/resolver && wrangler secret put SPORTSRC_API_KEY
# Local dev:   add to workers/resolver/.dev.vars → SPORTSRC_API_KEY=<your_key>
# NOTE: This is NEVER a VITE_ variable. The Vite dev server proxies /api/* to
#       the local Wrangler dev server (localhost:8787) automatically, so no
#       frontend env variable is needed in either dev or production.
# SPORTSRC_API_KEY=  ← do NOT set here; use wrangler secret put (see above)
